# GitHub release after a fix

After a fix that changes what a user runs, publish the next GitHub release in the same turn. Do not wait to be asked.

## Skip when

- Doc-only edits, typos, or refactors with no behavior change.
- The user said not to release, or the change is an experiment that will be reverted.

## Version and notes

- Repo is [OswaldJO/GBear](https://github.com/OswaldJO/GBear). `origin` (`MacDeck`) redirects there. Tags are lightweight: `v1.1.6`, then the next patch.
- Before tagging, set `docs/source control log.md` and the **BJ-###** **Commit** field to that release (not *in progress*).
- Release notes match `build/release-assets/notes-v1.1.6.md`: what broke, what to install, and who needs it (host, friend, or both). Say to start the session again and send a new invite when the co-op link changed.

## Mac build

When Mac code changed, build a universal Release app. Use `CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='Apple Development'` (the full certificate name conflicts with automatic signing):

```bash
xcodebuild -project GBear.xcodeproj -scheme GBear -configuration Release \
  -destination 'generic/platform=macOS' ONLY_ACTIVE_ARCH=NO ARCHS='arm64 x86_64' \
  SYMROOT="$PWD/build" DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=AFYV687T82 \
  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='Apple Development' build
ditto -c -k --keepParent build/Release/GBear.app build/release-assets/GBear-macOS.zip
```

Confirm `lipo` shows `x86_64 arm64` and `codesign --verify --deep --strict` passes. The app is signed with the Apple Development certificate and is not notarized.

## Assets

Upload **GBear-macOS.zip** when the Mac app changed. Re-upload **GBear-companion-android.apk** and **GBearGuest-windows.exe** from the previous release when those apps did not change, so the page still has all three. Rebuild an app only when its code changed.

Do not commit `build/`.

## Publish

Commit the fix and the doc update, tag `vX.Y.Z` on that commit, push `HEAD` and the tag, then create the release with those assets. Use `gh` when it is installed. Otherwise call the GitHub API with the existing git credential and do not print the token.

Return the release URL.
